  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Ebi Fry",
  "text": "Ebi Fry\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n6 black tiger prawns,\n\na pinch of salt,\n\n1 tbsp potato starch,\n\nwater\n\nBatter\n\n1 egg\n\n? tbsp water,\n\n2 tbsp flour,\n\n80g Nama Panko (moist bread crumbs)\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Shell the prawns, leaving the tail. Pierce the back of the prawn with a skewer, and remove the salt vein. Remove the sharp pointed scales from the tail and trim.\n\n2. Add a little salt to the prawns, dust with potato starch, add water and mix.\n\n3. Rinse the prawns.\n\n4. Dry the prawns on a paper towel.\n\n5. Score the stomach of the prawns diagonally and, from the back, break the resistance of the body with your fingers to stop them curling when cooked.\n\n6. Season the prawns with salt.\n\n7. Beat the egg in a bowl and add a little water.\n\n8. Roll the prawns in the flour, dip in the egg and coat with breadcrumbs.\n\n9. Deep fry.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
